            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recent studies have identified patients with unstable angina and increased troponin I or T as a high risk population gaining benefit from adjunctive treatment with glycoprotein IIb/IIIa receptor antagonists and early reperfusion by coronary interventions.</AbstractText>
